      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Cherryville Historical Museum, a treasure trove of local history, opened to the public in 1995 and remains a key cultural landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitcherryville.com/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The former Beam's Shell Service Station, now the Grier Beam Truck Museum, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places and showcases vintage trucking history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherryville%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Originally settled in 1762, the crossroads town was known as White Pine before its name changed to Cherryville.",
